// XFAIL: RT-475: WRONG CODE: a program's trait implemented for [i64] with methods named len and is_empty takes `s.len()` and `s.is_empty()` of an `s: &[i64]` from the slice's inherent methods: vole prints `8 true`; rustc's probe prefers the inherent method at the same step and prints `3 false` (0.30.2)
// From the review of the method-probe work (g302probe2). Since v0.30.1 at least.
// RT-430c and RT-431 are a blanket impl's len on an array and in std's
// bodies; here the impl is for [i64] alone and the call is the program's.
// first: rt_475b (a Vec too), rt_475c; an impl for &[i64]: rt_475d.
// EXPECT: 3 false
trait L {
    fn len(&self) -> i64;
    fn is_empty(&self) -> bool;
}

impl L for [i64] {
    fn len(&self) -> i64 {
        8
    }

    fn is_empty(&self) -> bool {
        true
    }
}

fn main() -> i32 {
    let a = [1i64, 2, 3];
    let s: &[i64] = &a;
    println("{} {}", s.len(), s.is_empty());
    0
}
